Z||000000||HotFieroGT||10-30-1999||12:31 AM||||Are the engine numbers unique to each car or is there a series of numbers that are unique to each year for the Fiero?  I am just curious if someone can tell if you do not have the original engine that came with the car from the factory by looking at the number on the block.  ||||reg||3
Z||000001||Tim||10-30-1999||11:48 AM||||I can't remember the source for this info, when I do I'll post the source.<P>Fiero Engine Stamping Information<BR>1985   2.8   CBX, CBY<BR>1986   2.8   DAF, DAH, DBN<BR>1987   2.8   SCN, SCP<BR>1988   2.8   CFC, CFD<BR>Engine number location: front of block below right cylinder head. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Boxdin||10-31-1999||10:25 PM||||Hey Tim<P><BR>I know external brackets differ between years, but are all these engine #'s listed identical in terms of being 2.8 HO's  equal internally and in power?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tim||10-31-1999||10:43 PM||||Yes?  All these numbers are for the L44 V6.(HO)<P>I think these numbers are used by GM during vehicle assembly.<P>When the Corvette people say they have matching numbers this is the engine part of the numbers.<P>||||reg||1
